  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When migrating data from a fedora 4 to 6 repository using the following steps:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://wiki.lyrasis.org/display/FEDORA6x/Migrate+to+Fedora+6#MigratetoFedora6-TheFedora4%E2%86%926MigrationPath"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If the fedora 4 instance being exported does not have the same hostname as the fedora 6 instance being migrated to, it will result in triples being created in Fedora 6 with the original Fedora 4 URL as the subject. The result is that the triples are not directly describing the Fedora 6 resource, and will display in the “Other resources” section.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The issue is that fcrepo-import-export tool exports RDF with the original subjects, but the fcrepo-upgrade-util does not have a way to remap those URLs for the new fcrepo 6 instance. Since the subjects are from another base url, fcrepo 6 does not interpret them as referring to the resource being created.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We could address this by adding a base url remapping option to fcrepo-upgrade-utils, similar to the fcrepo-import-export tools --map option.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
