  "description": "<p>When migrating data from a fedora 4 to 6 repository using the following steps:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.lyrasis.org/display/FEDORA6x/Migrate+to+Fedora+6#MigratetoFedora6-TheFedora4%E2%86%926MigrationPath\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.lyrasis.org/display/FEDORA6x/Migrate+to+Fedora+6#MigratetoFedora6-TheFedora4%E2%86%926MigrationPath</a> </p>\n\n<p>If the fedora 4 instance being exported does not have the same hostname as the fedora 6 instance being migrated to, it will result in triples being created in Fedora 6 with the original Fedora 4 URL as the subject. The result is that the triples are not directly describing the Fedora 6 resource, and will display in the “Other resources” section.</p>\n\n<p>The issue is that fcrepo-import-export tool exports RDF with the original subjects, but the fcrepo-upgrade-util does not have a way to remap those URLs for the new fcrepo 6 instance. Since the subjects are from another base url, fcrepo 6 does not interpret them as referring to the resource being created.</p>\n\n<p>We could address this by adding a base url remapping option to fcrepo-upgrade-utils, similar to the fcrepo-import-export tools --map option.</p>",
